This isn't an uuencoded file, and it obviously doesn't contain a picture....
On the other hand, when someone posts with "Playmate June '93" in the
subject line, and by Gods, there is a uuencoded picture in there, a
reasonable person is going to presume that the picture is what it claims 
to be.  As well they should.

A reasonable person doesn't have to prove <anything> before removing the
posting and/or the poster's net.privileges in that case.  Net access is 
not a civil right, at least not yet, and in nearly all cases is provided
under a specific set of terms and conditions.

>I think Playboy is entitled to have its rights regarding
>copyrighted material respected.  I don't think copyrights
>should be violated.  I hope that's clear enough.  
