Actually, no.  My larger problem is abps, not abpe.  abpe is a problem, 
but abps is worse.  I haven't seen a legit picture <ever> in there.  I cut
it at roughly the same time I did abpe, and for the same reason.

Soc.men?  Other groups?  Sure, people post things there sometimes that are
out-and-out ripoffs.  They usually get resoundingly shouted down and letters
get sent to sysadmins.  People get rebuked and even lose their access over
these activities, especially for repeat offenses.  That never seems to 
happen in apbe and apbs.  Why?

Because people on the net who read those groups are ethically bankrupt and
want the pictures, stolen or not.  To put it bluntly, the readers of those
groups don't give a tinker's damn whether or not the pictures are legally
acquired and posted.  Just look in abped today, and you'll see people asking
for GIFs by the <name> of the porn star!  

Hint: Porn stars don't pose for free or allow public distribution of their 
works without compensation.

I have not seen <one> post in reply to the "wanna-jackoff-material" today 
saying that the material they're asking for is copyrighted and should not 
be posted.  In fact, there is usually no such response to these messages.

>Today's (January 2, 1993) Boston Globe business section reports
>on a number of organized attempts to defend copyright.  They do
