Let's clear up a few misconceptions here:

First of all the CICA archives run on an SGI Challenge M R4000 server
that has 96MB of memory and 13GB of disk space. This is hardly old
equipment and it is owned by Indiana University, not Mike Regoli.  It
also runs on the University's network, not on Mike Regoli's private
internet feed.

Secondly the network traffic generated by our ftp archives constitutes
~20% of our T1 links to the internet (CICnet to be exact).  This is a
very _NON_ significant percentage of our bandwith.  It has not escaped
the notice of the higher administration.

Next, contrary to Greg Travis's belief, I have spent (and continue to
spend) many hours supporting the archive.  Thus CICA/IU devotes part of its
