Hello,

Due to the recent ongoing discussion regarding the censorship issues around
"Fanny Hill", I've been *inundated* with requests from people wanting to know
where it is located, and who didn't see my original set of postings describing
where to find it (they have no doubt expired at many sites).  And with the
next U.S. News and World Report mentioning my particular publication of "Fanny
Hill" in a larger article regarding the Internet (don't know the exact subject
but it may have to do with censorship issues), I want this post in place so
those who become interested can easily locate "Fanny Hill".

"Fanny Hill" can be found in two versions:  a Windows 3.1 Help file format
with hypertext capabilities, and a plain-vanilla ASCII text file.  The main
anonymous ftp site to download it is:

netcom.com   /pub/noring/fanny  ...  (the files are fanny10.zip and ascii.txt)

The Windows 3.1 Help format version (which is quite nice! give it a try) is
copyrighted Shareware.  The ASCII file is public domain and free.  The ASCII
file can also be found at the site ftp.spies.com  /Library/Classics .

[Canadians take note:  Because of the recent flury of repressive laws in Canada
regarding sexual material, which are based on the almost unbelievable 1991
Butler decision, owning a copy of Fanny Hill in Canada (not the U.S. however!)
*may be* illegal.  Thus, I do not authorize the distribution of Fanny Hill
into Canada and if you do happen to obtain a copy, by whatever means, you are
totally responsible for the possession of it.]

Enjoy "Fanny Hill"!

Jon Noring

(p.s., if you don't have anonymous ftp access, then I will email upon request
only the Help file version, file fanny10.zip, in 11 parts in uuencoded form,
