Unless there's a notice on the image *stating* that it has been released
into the public domain, it is not public domain. That's been the law since
March of 88. The image is copyrighted by whoever took the photo. There's
also the not so minor detail that you are required to keep records of
your models under federal law. And include a notice as to where the records
may be examined. That's part of the "kiddie porn" law. 

>They never mention the sound newsgroups.  They don't even
>mention the other binary newsgroups.  All they see are the SEX newsgroups.
