There have been *lots* of suits about Playboy and the like *images* being 
pirated (mostly by print folks, not BBSes). We are only *now* getting
suits over copyright violations involving sounds. But Those look to be
real doozies. CompuServe is being sued over *MIDI* files! That's right,
not even digitized sounds, but someone's attempt at doing his own
*arrangement* of a copyrighted work.

And guess what? Just as the "ddomsayers" have been saying all along
the lawyer stated that they were going after the system rather than the
users because the users are too scattered, but they *know* how to get hold
of the system. That statement is a sysadmins worst nightmare come true.

